    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8198fa91-fbc5-5fdb-ac60-f8d73a0a6f2c",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186096700/caller-moderate/generated/65fe99f9b62e2e5c94dbb04627f3bcc749380277ad843812bd34f36ad1e5e52e.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{c}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{c}\\ne -2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{b}$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{d}$. So, $\\mathbf{b}=-\\mathbf{d}$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{a}$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{c}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{c}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "aa2734e0-0fef-5e2c-bae5-67d377e600cb",
          ":answer-field/key": "$\\mathbf{c}=-2\\mathbf{a}$",
